Accept the commands Music Assistant actually advertises.

The server lists `seek` and `seek_relative` in a controller's
supported_commands, and the vendored MediaCommand enum has neither. One
unknown member invalidates ControllerStatePayload, which invalidates
ServerStatePayload, which discards the whole ServerStateMessage - 606 of
them on this device. The session's volume, mute, repeat, shuffle and
capability list go with each one.

Colour and metadata are NOT lost with them, which is worth knowing before
treating this as urgent: the server sends those in their own state
messages, and measurement during Spotify Connect playback showed palettes
arriving normally while these failures continued.

seek_max_ms rides in the same object and has no field on the model.

--- a/aiosendspin/models/types.py
+++ b/aiosendspin/models/types.py
@@ -175,6 +175,11 @@
     SHUFFLE = "shuffle"
     UNSHUFFLE = "unshuffle"
     SWITCH = "switch"
+    # Music Assistant advertises both of these in supported_commands.
+    # Without them one unknown member invalidates the whole
+    # ControllerStatePayload, and with it every server/state message.
+    SEEK = "seek"
+    SEEK_RELATIVE = "seek_relative"
 
 
 class PictureFormat(Enum):
--- a/aiosendspin/models/controller.py
+++ b/aiosendspin/models/controller.py
@@ -61,7 +61,7 @@
     supported_commands: list[MediaCommand]
     """
     Subset of: play, pause, stop, next, previous, volume, mute, repeat_off, repeat_one,
-    repeat_all, shuffle, unshuffle, switch.
+    repeat_all, shuffle, unshuffle, switch, seek, seek_relative.
     """
     volume: int
     """Volume of the whole group, range 0-100."""
@@ -71,6 +71,8 @@
     """Repeat mode: 'off' = no repeat, 'one' = repeat current track, 'all' = repeat all."""
     shuffle: bool
     """Whether shuffle is enabled."""
+    seek_max_ms: int | None = None
+    """Furthest position the session can seek to, in milliseconds."""
 
     def __post_init__(self) -> None:
         """Validate field values."""
